According to ISO 45001:2018, the requirement to apply the **hierarchy of controls** is found in **Clause 8.1.2 - Elimination of hazards and reduction of OH&S risks**.

Specifically, **subclause 8.1.2 c)** states:

> "The organization shall establish, implement and maintain a process(es) for the **elimination of hazards and reduction of OH&S risks** using the following hierarchy of controls:
> 1) eliminate the hazard;
> 2) substitute with less hazardous processes, operations, materials or equipment;
> 3) use engineering controls;
> 4) use administrative controls, including training;
> 5) use adequate personal protective equipment."

Therefore, when planning to meet OH&S objectives, address audit findings, or handle incidents, you must apply this hierarchy to determine the most effective risk reduction measures. The clause emphasizes that the hierarchy is a core methodology for risk treatment, prioritizing permanent solutions (like elimination) over those that merely control the risk (like PPE).
